      "keyInsight": "We hide our flaws because we think exposure will destroy us. But isolation is actually what fuels the poison. Think of toxic shame like damp mold growing in a dark, sealed closet. It only spreads when the doors stay shut. The moment you open the door and let fresh air in, the mold dies. You think perfection earns love, but real connection requires showing your cracks. When you reveal your true self to someone safe, the monster under the bed vanishes into thin air.",
