      "keyInsight": "Healthy shame sounds like a contradiction, but it is actually your internal check engine light. It simply tells you that you are human, not a flawless robot. Toxic shame, on the other hand, says you are complete garbage. Healing is not about pretending you are godlike and invincible. It is about learning to accept your natural human limits. When your dashboard light flashes, you do not abandon the vehicle by the highway. You pull into the service bay, grab your wrench, and fix the leak.",
